{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["And Miriam the prophetess took, etc. — and similar is ״כאשר צוה יהוה את משה ויניחהו אהרן לפני העדות למשמרת״. And likewise in Jeremiah: ״כי בא ירמיה אל בית הבור ואל החנויות וישב שם ירמיה ימים רבים וישלח המלך צדקיהו ויקחהו״." "The prophetess — one who speaks words of praise or reproof to people." "Sister of Aharon — she is called 'sister' after the firstborn, as I explained at ״אחות נביות״ and ״אחות לוטן״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "Rashbam cites these parallel verses to illustrate that the verb לקח ('took') can refer to a person being fetched or stationed, not only to taking an object.", 1 "Rashbam defines נביאה here not as one who predicts the future but as one who speak divine words of praise or rebuke."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:42.302001864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}